  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Dry weather will persist through Saturday, then \nchances for rain return Sunday through Monday.\n\nExpansive surface high pressure across eastern Ontario and Quebec \nwill remain in place through Saturday morning before drifting east \nto Labrador Sunday. Subsidence and dry air associated with this high \nwill continue to support dry weather areawide tonight through \nSaturday, although there will be more high clouds than the past few \ndays.\n\nMeanwhile, an unseasonably strong coastal low off the Delmarva \ntonight will remain in place through Saturday while maturing and \noccluding. The coastal low will then complete a cyclonic loop to the \nsouth of Long Island Saturday night through Sunday, nearing the \nJersey shore by late Sunday and Sunday night. The westward drift in \nthe position of the vertically stacked low will advect Atlantic \nmoisture westward across NY/PA, with thickening and lowering clouds. \nThe first chance of showers will reach Central NY Sunday morning, \nthen progress gradually westward as an inverted trough axis north of \nthe low center rotates westward. Showers may reach the Genesee \nValley and western Finger Lakes by early to mid afternoon. Far \nwestern NY should stay dry most of Sunday, although a few light \nshowers may arrive by late afternoon or evening given the westward \ntrend in recent model guidance.\n\nThe coastal low is then forecast to slowly meander northeast along \nthe New England coast Sunday night through Tuesday, weakening with \ntime. The greatest rain chances and greatest western extent of the \nrain shield will be Sunday night, with showers then gradually \ntapering off and ending from west to east Monday through Monday \nnight as the low weakens and moves northeast. Mainly dry weather \nwill return for most of the area by Tuesday, and Tuesday night for \nthe North Country.",
